WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:02.050 line:88% position:50% align:middle
Here is what happens

2
00:00:02.050 --> 00:00:03.950 line:88% position:50% align:middle
inside a Kangen water ionizer.

3
00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:06.450 line:88% position:50% align:middle
After tap water passes

4
00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:07.690 line:88% position:50% align:middle
through an external pre-filter,

5
00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:09.480 line:88% position:50% align:middle
it enters the machine's

6
00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:10.850 line:88% position:50% align:middle
internal filtration stage,

7
00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:12.820 line:88% position:50% align:middle
where remaining chlorine,

8
00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:14.330 line:88% position:50% align:middle
rust, and sediment are reduced

9
00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:16.690 line:88% position:50% align:middle
before the water reaches electrolysis.

10
00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:18.710 line:88% position:50% align:middle
Inside that chamber,

11
00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:20.370 line:88% position:50% align:middle
water flows between plates.

12
00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:22.430 line:88% position:50% align:middle
A controlled direct current

13
00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:24.430 line:88% position:50% align:middle
creates an electric field.

14
00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:26.390 line:88% position:50% align:middle
That field drives reactions

15
00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:28.350 line:88% position:50% align:middle
at the plate surfaces

16
00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:30.220 line:88% position:50% align:middle
and guides dissolved ions

17
00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:32.650 line:88% position:50% align:middle
toward the opposite charge.

18
00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:35.370 line:88% position:50% align:middle
The process produces two streams:

19
00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:38.210 line:88% position:50% align:middle
a more alkaline cathode stream,

20
00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:41.030 line:88% position:50% align:middle
and a more acidic anode stream.

21
00:00:42.490 --> 00:00:44.090 line:88% position:50% align:middle
Positively charged minerals,

22
00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:45.590 line:88% position:50% align:middle
including calcium and magnesium,

23
00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:47.830 line:88% position:50% align:middle
sodium, and potassium,

24
00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:49.990 line:88% position:50% align:middle
move toward the cathode.

25
00:00:49.990 --> 00:00:53.750 line:88% position:50% align:middle
At the cathode, water is reduced,

26
00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:56.990 line:88% position:50% align:middle
producing hydrogen and hydroxide ions.

27
00:00:57.770 --> 00:00:59.490 line:88% position:50% align:middle
Dissolved hydrogen may remain

28
00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:00.810 line:88% position:50% align:middle
in the alkaline stream,

29
00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:03.430 line:88% position:50% align:middle
while hydroxide raises its pH.

30
00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:08.230 line:88% position:50% align:middle
Meanwhile, negatively charged ions,

31
00:01:08.230 --> 00:01:10.230 line:88% position:50% align:middle
including carbonate and sulfate,

32
00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:12.950 line:88% position:50% align:middle
move toward the anode.

33
00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:15.990 line:88% position:50% align:middle
At that surface, water is oxidized,

34
00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:18.490 line:88% position:50% align:middle
producing oxygen and hydrogen ions,

35
00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:21.130 line:88% position:50% align:middle
which lower the acidic stream's pH.

36
00:01:21.130 --> 00:01:24.250 line:88% position:50% align:middle
This is the core of water ionization:

37
00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:26.350 line:88% position:50% align:middle
filtration first,

38
00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:28.870 line:88% position:50% align:middle
then controlled electrochemistry,

39
00:01:28.870 --> 00:01:29.570 line:88% position:50% align:middle
creating two streams.
